# CodeScene Refactoring Standards

For refactoring work, use CodeScene MCP as the objective quality guide when the `codescene` MCP server is available.

Before refactoring:
- Run `codescene.code_health_review` on the target file or files.
- Capture `codescene.code_health_score` so the work has a measurable baseline.

During refactoring:
- Prefer small, reviewable steps that reduce responsibility, nesting, coupling, and hard-to-follow control flow.
- Do not treat formatting, renaming, or cosmetic cleanup alone as a meaningful Code Health improvement.

After each meaningful step:
- Re-run `codescene.code_health_review` to confirm the issue improved and no regression was introduced.
- Use `codescene.code_health_score` as the compact trend check.

Success means Code Health improves or at minimum does not decline, structure is clearer, and no new technical debt is introduced.

Source: https://github.com/codescene-oss/codescene-mcp-server/tree/ce49139c4528287a0191d50a18e8af38cf7a4f10/.amazonq/rules
